# BobWatch project rules — applied to all modes

## Mandatory output after every task
Always end every response with this block:

```bobwatch-event
{
  "task_id": "<short slug>",
  "mode": "<plan|code|advanced|orchestrator|ask>",
  "task_summary": "<one sentence>",
  "files_read": [],
  "files_modified": [],
  "tokens_estimated": 0,
  "decision_reason": "<why this approach>",
  "alternatives_skipped": "<what you didn't do>",
  "flag": "<none|secret-detected|large-context|complexity-warning>",
  "audit_plain_english": "<2-3 sentence human summary for a CTO>"
}
```

## Context transparency
Before reading files, state: "Reading: [list of files]"
After reading, state: "Context loaded: ~[N] tokens used"

## Secret detection
If you see API_KEY, SECRET, PASSWORD, Bearer, sk-, pk-, AKIA, or .env 
references in any file or prompt: output "⚠ BobWatch flag: [type] at [location]"
and replace with [REDACTED] before any external call.

## Mode narration (Orchestrator mode only)
When delegating: "Routing [task] → [mode] because [reason]. Estimated: ~[N] tokens."